{
  "id": "05-love-creation",
  "title": "Love Your Neighbor and Creation",
  "tenet": "Care for what God has entrusted",
  "durationMs": 44208,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/05-love-creation.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/05-love-creation.json",
  "text": "One morning, a girl noticed that the garden beside her street had become a place for rubbish. She could not restore it in a day. She began by clearing one small patch and inviting a friend to help. Love takes responsibility for what is within reach. Following Jesus turns us toward people and toward the world God has entrusted to our care. Feed, listen, forgive, protect, repair, and share. Refuse waste when a better choice is possible. Care for a person without expecting applause. Care for a living place without waiting for someone else to begin. A life of service grows through repeated small acts. Plant something good in the garden each day. Aim for a plentiful harvest.",
